      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"table_name\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"count\": 16, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_3887\", \"name\": \"IAP Max Enrollment 12 Activities with Enrollment-Unit Difference and Department Subject Counts\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects with a maximum enrollment of 12, show the activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, subject title, the difference between the maximum enrollment and the total units, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the number of subjects in the same department, for each subject offered in the same term and where the school code and subject title are not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3215\", \"name\": \"2012 Subjects Department Row Numbers with Subject Code School Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012, show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code, for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3867\", \"name\": \"Subject Code Department Counts Matched with 2022FA Above-Average Unit Running Sums\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_50\", \"name\": \"2021 Non-Graduate-Credit Math Undergraduate Catalog Subjects Offered by Science School Count\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects offered in 2021 that are not for graduate credit, are listed as undergraduate in the course catalog, are in the Mathematics department, and are also offered by the School of Science? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1302\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Department 2007 Course Rollup with Department Unit Totals and Latest-Year Course Counts\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each course offered by a degree-granting department in the School of Engineering, except for the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department, in the 2007 academic year, what is the course key, course name, department name, the number of catalog subjects, the total units for those subjects, and for each department, include a grand total for all courses in the format of (null, null, department name, total subjects, total units)? Additionally, for each such department, what is the total number of units for courses in the \\\"Engineering\\\" or \\\"Non-MIT\\\" schools (where the total units for the department is greater than 1000 and the department is not \\\"Political Science\\\"), and how many distinct courses did the department offer in the most recent academic year available? Present the results as: course key, course name, department name, number of catalog subjects, total units for those subjects, department total units, and number of distinct courses in the latest year, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1335\", \"name\": \"Union of Math 2008 Unit Range-Variance with Long Descriptions and High Average Unit Department Stddev\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1766\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Level Counts with Min Units, Course Options, and Highest Term Average Library Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2210\", \"name\": \"Math Subject Code School Ranks Matched with 2024 Catalog Offerings and Department Min Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code in degree-granting departments where the department is Mathematics, and for subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, rank of the subject code within each school name group ordered by subject code, subject ID, subject number, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the subject description from the CIS course catalog, ordered by school name, rank, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2272\", \"name\": \"Math Department Unit Statistics with Course Level Student Counts and Lecture-Lab Unit Averages\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2335\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Level Counts with Catalog Unit Stddev and Unique Subject Codes\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2365\", \"name\": \"Top 3 Most Offered Math Courses per Term with Description Counts, Min CIP Code, and Department Phone\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 3 most frequently offered courses in the Mathematics department, for each course and each term it was offered, display the course number, course description, subject title, number of times offered, department name, number of unique course descriptions for that course and department, the minimum CIP program code for that course and department, the term code, the term description, the school name, and the department phone number. Do not repeat the course number if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by course number and term code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2377\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Unit Range-Variance with Offered-This-Year Subjects and Responsible Faculty Contact Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Faculty Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department's name, the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the academic year 2022 and that are also listed in the CIS course catalog, and for all course subjects in the catalog where the department code is 18 (Mathematics), the department name is 'Mathematics', and the subject is offered this year, show the subject code, subject number, responsible faculty's full name, Moira list member, the average office phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the responsible faculty's last name and ordered by the subject code, and the email address of the responsible faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3163\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Course Level Counts with Min Total Units and Design-Unit Course Counts\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting and the total units are greater than 6, provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units offered, and the number of courses where the design units are at least 3. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3311\", \"name\": \"Status-U Library Subjects with Enrollment Matched with Department Offered-This-Year Unit Dispersion\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3590\", \"name\": \"Union of Subject Code School Dense Ranks and 2012SU Cluster-S Subject Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show, for each subject, the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null; and for subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title. Indicate the source of each row as either 'Subq1' or 'Subq2'. List all results together, showing the columns: subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, dense rank by school, offer department name, total units, row number window, and source, in that order, ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5279\", \"name\": \"2014JA Cross-Enrollment and Chemistry Subjects Listed as Offered in Academic Year Count\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects offered in the 2014 January term by the Harvard Cross-Enrollment Program and the Chemistry department are listed in the course catalog as being offered in the academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
