2. Lineage & Relationships\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION → joins SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE`), SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (`COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE`), CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (graph edge confirmed); joined *by* COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, CIP.\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY → joined by SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT`), SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT; member of `concept_person_directory`.\n- CIS_COURSE_CATALOG → 16 dependent metrics (metrics_by_table), joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT via `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (dw_3163, dw_1335, dw_2272 SQL).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. TOTAL_UNITS source candidates:**\n\n| Dimension | CIS_COURSE_CATALOG | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | academic year × term × subject (catalog feed) | subject offering per term/section | subject per term (registrar rollup) |\n| Dept key | DEPARTMENT_CODE (dw_3163 SQL) | DEPARTMENT_CODE (dw_2151 SQL) | OFFER_DEPT_CODE (dw_1335 SQL) |\n| Wording fit | \"**course** ... total units > 6\" precedents: dw_3163, dw_1766, dw_2272, dw_3311 (\"total units of **courses offered by that department**\") | \"**subjects** offered by that department\" precedents: dw_2151, dw_4387 | \"subjects offered\" precedents: dw_1335, dw_2240 |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- \"maximum total units of any **course** offered by that department > 6\": CIS_COURSE_CATALOG — SUPPORTED (4 precedents with \"course\"+units, two with the exact \">6\" threshold); COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED — SUPPORTED but precedents word it \"subjects\"; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY — SUPPORTED but precedents word it \"subjects\".\n- \"name of the school that **department belongs to**\": SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME — SUPPORTED (column desc verbatim); SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.SCHOOL_NAME — \"school offering the course\" (different wording); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME — offering school.\n- \"student's full name, email address\": MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY — SUPPORTED (only student table with both).\n- \"course description, course level\": SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION — SUPPORTED (only table with COURSE_DESCRIPTION + COURSE_LEVEL pair; used by all 5 EECS precedents).\n- \"most common student year ... for each course level\": MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR partitioned by SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL — SUPPORTED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"students in the 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' department\" anchors to the exact literal used in dw_3969/dw_4458/dw_1474 filters (`DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'`; column_concept_department_name confirms this academic-name variant). \"For each department … and for students in EECS …\" matches the dw_3969 template whose gold SQL joins the two subqueries `ON s1.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s2.DEPARTMENT_CODE` (same for dw_1474, dw_4458) — the department-code join is the documented combination rule; a cross join has no precedent for this wording shape.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** \"total units > 6 per department/course-level\": 2 precedents, both CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (dw_3163, dw_1766). \"total units of courses offered by that department\": 1 precedent, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (dw_3311). EECS student+course-description+course-level block: 5 precedents (dw_3969, dw_4458, dw_1474, dw_2240, dw_1983), all using SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY with `t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t2.DEPARTMENT`.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nSIS_DEPARTMENT is the hub dimension (school attribution, degree-granting filters) in nearly all department metrics; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY serves per-department student listing questions; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION serves course-level/description questions; CIS_COURSE_CATALOG serves department-level course unit statistics.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated via semantic_get/semantic_graph: SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (metrics_by_table), column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, concepts (department_dimension, person_directory, subject_offering_facts, course_catalog_sources), metrics dw_3969, dw_4458, dw_1474, dw_2240, dw_1983, dw_3163, dw_1766, dw_3311, dw_1335, dw_2151, dw_2272, dw_4387. Remaining Phase-1 hits (facilities/space/time/IAP/library entities) were screened as unrelated to departments-courses-students except as noted. **mysql_query was attempted 9 times; all failed with `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` — execution verification was impossible.**\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** Part 1: SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ CIS_COURSE_CATALOG on DEPARTMENT_CODE, `GROUP BY` department, `HAVING MAX(TOTAL_UNITS) > 6`, selecting DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(TOTAL_UNITS), SCHOOL_NAME. Part 2: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY filtered to EECS (exact dw_3969 pattern). Mode of STUDENT_YEAR per COURSE_LEVEL via two-level window (COUNT OVER partition, then FIRST_VALUE ordered by count desc). Combine with `JOIN ON DEPARTMENT_CODE` per the three EECS precedents.\n\n**6b/6c.** Data: join keys are documented code-level keys (no fan-out beyond the intended student×course pairing). Semantic-network: SCHOOL_NAME column desc matches the question verbatim; total_units decision guide + 4 \"course\"-worded precedents favor CIS_COURSE_CATALOG. Business: dw_3969 is the near-identical question template. Caveat: DB unreachable, so no runtime verification; deterministic tie-break (`STUDENT_YEAR`) added for the mode.\n\n",
